# Two more GLM53_TF_TOOL_FIXES names (0620's knob; both in `all`, so off when it is unset and on in prod.env's `all`):
# - opencalls: when the model's end token (not a stop string, not the token limit) ended the answer inside a GLM
#   <tool_call> with no </tool_call>, the call is returned (finish_reason tool_calls) only when it is complete but for
#   that tag: no argument value open (the model wrote every </arg_value> itself; a value is never closed here), one
#   whole call to an offered tool (a name, then only <arg_key>/<arg_value> pairs), and, after the optional argkeys
#   repair, every parameter in the tool's `required` present (a bare name: only a tool that requires none). Only
#   </tool_call> is ever added. Anything else stays the reply's text, as before, and nothing runs: fail-closed,
#   because a value cut mid-string (a shell command, a path) executed as a call is the dangerous case. (This tree
#   never dropped that markup: the non-streamed content and the streamed final delta carried it.) A call the token
#   limit cut, and a reply a stop string ended, are unchanged. Streamed and non-streamed replies take the same
#   result (App.run).
# - argkeys: a GLM call whose <arg_key> the model left out (`read path</arg_key><arg_value>..`, or
#   `</arg_value>\npath</arg_key>`) gets it back before parsing (repair_glm_keys); before, the whole block was
#   not a call and came back as text.
# Semantics from MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold patch 0055-glm-open-tool-calls (issue #22,
# Apache-2.0; repair_glm_keys copied as written), re-implemented for this tree's end parser and narrowed: 0055 also
# closes an open value and does not check `required`. No streaming call parser here, so 0055's GlmCallStreamer part
# has no counterpart.
#
